#%PAM-1.0

# =============================================================================
# OpenDoas PAM Configuration Template
# =============================================================================
# This file configures the Pluggable Authentication Modules (PAM) for OpenDoas.
# It defines how authentication is handled, specifically focusing on session
# management for resource limits and standard authentication stacks.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session Management: User Limits
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: The PAM module used for setting user limits (e.g., max
# processes, open files) defined in /etc/security/limits.conf.
# This is a required session module, meaning the limit setup must succeed
# for the session to proceed.
#
# Variable: pam_mod
# Schema Default: 'pam_limits.so'
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
session    required   {{ pam_mod | default('pam_limits.so') }}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication Stack: Common Auth
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: Includes the common authentication PAM configuration.
# This typically handles username/password verification or other
# primary authentication methods configured in /etc/pam.d/common-auth.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@include common-auth

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Account Management: Common Account
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: Includes the common account PAM configuration.
# This handles account validity checks (e.g., account expiration,
# access restrictions) as defined in /etc/pam.d/common-account.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@include common-account

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session Management: Common Session (Non-Interactive)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description: Includes the common non-interactive session PAM configuration.
# This handles setup/teardown for sessions that do not require a terminal,
# such as sudo/doas commands executed in scripts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@include common-session-noninteractive
